meta {
  name: Initialize
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/donate
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "amount": 900,
    "email": "maximilianogbuabor@gmail.com",
    "name": "kolbe",
    "comment": "Love your work",
    "supportAreas": ["FUND_BOOTCAMP", "SPONSOR_ASH_BENEFICIARY"]
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Initialize Donation
  
  Initializes a donation transaction via the Paystack payment gateway. Returns an authorization URL that the client should redirect the donor to in order to complete payment.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `POST /api/v1/donate`
  
  ## Authorization
  None — this is a public endpoint.
  
  ## Request Body (`JSON`)
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | `amount` | number | Yes | Donation amount in Naira. Minimum of 100 (₦100). Converted to kobo server-side. |
  | `email` | string | Yes | Email address of the donor. Must be a valid email. |
  | `name` | string | Yes | Name of the donor. Minimum 3 characters. |
  | `comment` | string | No | Optional message or comment from the donor. |
  | `supportAreas` | string[] | No | Areas the donor wishes to support (see allowed values below). Accepts a single string or an array. |
  
  ### Allowed `supportAreas` Values
  | Value | Description |
  | :--- | :--- |
  | `SPONSOR_ASH_BENEFICIARY` | Sponsor an ASH program beneficiary. |
  | `SPONSOR_TACOTS_BENEFICIARY` | Sponsor a TACOTS program beneficiary. |
  | `FUND_BOOTCAMP` | Fund a bootcamp initiative. |
  | `FUND_TEACHER_REFRESHER_COURSE` | Fund teacher refresher courses. |
  | `FUND_YOUTH_INITIATIVE` | Fund youth-focused initiatives. |
  | `DONATE_OUTREACH_EVENTS_AND_MATERIALS` | Donate towards outreach events and materials. |
  | `OTHER` | Other support area. |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "Transaction initialized successfully",
      "data": {
        "status": true,
        "message": "Authorization URL created",
        "data": {
          "authorization_url": "https://checkout.paystack.com/qipcu83p8nb8hw8",
          "access_code": "qipcu83p8nb8hw8",
          "reference": "i1lau8r7l0"
        }
      }
    }
    ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., amount below 100, invalid email, name too short).
  - **429 Too Many Requests**: Rate limit exceeded (`donationLimiter`: 5 requests per 10-minute window, keyed by IP).
  - **500 Internal Server Error**: Paystack API call failed.
  
  ## Rate Limiting
  This endpoint is protected by `donationLimiter` — a maximum of **5 requests per 10-minute window**, keyed by the client's IP address. Exceeds return a `429` with `{ code: "RATE_LIMITED", message: "Too many donation attempts. Please try again in 10 minutes" }`.
  
  ## Notes
  - The `amount` is transformed from Naira to kobo (multiplied by 100) before being sent to Paystack.
  - On successful payment, the donor is redirected to the configured `PAYSTACK_CALLBACK` URL with a `reference` query parameter.
  - The `supportAreas` field is passed through to Paystack as part of the transaction `metadata` and is persisted to the `donors` table upon successful verification.
}
